# Monthly IFRS 9 batch: 06:00 on the 2nd of every month, for the previous
# month-end. Install with `crontab -e` and change /path/to/ifrs9-ecl-engine.
#
#   minute hour day-of-month month day-of-week  command
#
# Notes:
# - In a crontab line, % means "newline" unless escaped, so every % in the
#   date command is written as \%.
# - date -d "<first of this month> -1 day" is the last day of last month.
# - On WSL, cron is not started automatically: run `sudo service cron start`.
# - The demo data's dates are historical (2019), so cron is here to show the
#   scheduling; scripts/run_all_months.sh is how the project is actually run.
# - The batch takes a lock, so a run that overlaps a slow previous one exits
#   at once instead of running twice.

0 6 2 * * cd /path/to/ifrs9-ecl-engine && ./scripts/run_monthly_batch.sh "$(date -d "$(date +\%Y-\%m-01) -1 day" +\%F)" >> logs/cron.log 2>&1
